## Changes from the reviewed round

- Remove annotation headers, the Context label, HTML paths and visible page-URL metadata. Keep the context selector and icon-only HTML navigation on one row; include Selection as a generic context option.
- Use two screenshot-offset spinboxes. Retain the screenshot and pointed bubble; metadata remains captured even when hidden from the editor.
- Restore compact review-comment rows with a type dropdown, comment, removal action and Add feedback. Multiple feedback items belong to one annotation.
- Keep Stack and Create wording independent of destination. Each batch item has its own destination; numbering is an external gutter. No global destination, header/close row or Keep collecting action.
- Show the same editor structure in overlay, embedded and batch hosts. The batch host supplies one Create action instead of repeating individual action footers; it is not a separate annotation editor.

## Reservations for review and implementation

- The standalone and embedded versions remain more spacious than the requested compact implementation. The batch is the better density reference; do not reproduce generous generated padding as a requirement.
- Image 0 labels its feedback choice Bug report rather than the requested Fix. This is generation drift, not a decision to change the review-comment taxonomy.
- Image 1's surrounding review-page layout and repeated title are incidental. It demonstrates embedding, not a redesign of the accepted review architecture.
- Images are static: open selectors overlapping previews do not establish actual overlay positioning or keyboard behavior. Context navigation, highlighting, URL-label resolution and coordinate handling still require implementation.
- Offset axes/units and pointer percentages must have explicit, distinct semantics. The pictured X/Y values are illustrative.
- Background text, avatars, timing values and tool totals contain generation drift. They do not change the accepted board/chat specifications or establish that the depicted preview bug was fixed.
- The compact typed feedback pattern was checked against the saved real review capture at `round4-final/review-context.png`. A distinct earlier PR-comment generated reference was not located; do not claim an exact match to that missing reference.
- Composer destinations persist an annotation and insert an ordinary URL/Markdown link into the draft; Create does not send a chat message. No custom annotation rendering is added to the MVP composer.
- Batch partial-failure/retry behavior remains implementation design work. Nothing was delivered to Inputs, review or chat during generation.

Exact generation instructions are retained in [prompts](prompts.md). Earlier rounds and their user corrections remain preserved.
